{
  "contract": "work-order",
  "about": "The work order (DOR-5063): computeWorkOrder({ items, projects, config, now }). Items and projects are written short and expanded by the test: an item is { id, p (priority 0-4), state (backlog | unstarted | started; default unstarted), size, project (a project id), labels, blockedBy, blocks, due (YYYY-MM-DD), created (ISO), triage, pin }; a project is { id, name, status, priority, target, labels }. 'base' is the shared fixture; each case may replace config.orderKeys and patch items. expected.issues is the issue order, best first; expected.held, needsTriage, inFlight and dorian list identifiers (held and needsTriage with their reason or missing fields); expected.inherits maps an item to the blocked item whose place it took; expected.banners is exact. Each flip changes one field of one item on the base and names where that item lands (place, or 'unranked: <reason>' as rankOfIssue prints it). The test also shuffles every input and demands the same output.",
